00:10:25.164 --> 00:10:28.740
who inspired you and encouraged
you to do your music.

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:30.314
Can you tell us a bit about her?

00:10:30.314 --> 00:10:32.923
- Well that's Lena McLin,
like my second mother.

00:10:32.923 --> 00:10:35.219
She's a pastor and everything.

00:10:35.219 --> 00:10:38.093
My music teacher in high school.

00:10:38.093 --> 00:10:40.309
In high school, my freshman year

00:10:40.309 --> 00:10:43.507
I was a, starting on
Kenwood's basketball team.

00:10:43.507 --> 00:10:46.065
That's the name of my high school.

00:10:46.065 --> 00:10:49.005
But I haven't had a music class.

00:10:49.005 --> 00:10:50.946
At that point in time I was,

00:10:50.946 --> 00:10:52.301
I think I was about 16, 17.

00:10:52.301 --> 00:10:54.460
I was not interested in music,

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.121
I was really trying to be

00:10:56.121 --> 00:10:58.523
the next Michael Jordan, of course.

00:10:58.523 --> 00:11:01.272
And she told me that I would sing,

00:11:01.272 --> 00:11:02.394
And she told me that I would sing,

00:11:02.394 --> 00:11:04.402
I would be the next Stevie Wonder

00:11:04.402 --> 00:11:05.812
I would be the next Stevie Wonder

00:11:05.812 --> 00:11:07.462
or superstar Michael Jackson
or something like that.

00:11:07.462 --> 00:11:09.105
or superstar Michael Jackson
or something like that.

00:11:09.105 --> 00:11:11.381
And I laughed at her like she was crazy.

00:11:11.381 --> 00:11:13.387
I was, I couldn't see it,

00:11:13.387 --> 00:11:14.476
I was, I couldn't see it.

00:11:14.476 --> 00:11:15.392
Everything I am today

00:11:15.392 --> 00:11:17.574
she could see it, my mother could see it

00:11:17.574 --> 00:11:21.384
and she would tell me that I was
going to be where I'm at today

00:11:21.384 --> 00:11:22.488
and even further.

00:11:22.488 --> 00:11:25.210
So and it just happened.

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:29.004
She put me in a talent show
and I did the talent show

00:11:29.004 --> 00:11:31.548
and the girls were
screaming and everything.

00:11:31.548 --> 00:11:32.858
And I was like, man,

00:11:32.858 --> 00:11:36.275
I don't get this kind
of love on the court.

00:11:37.495 --> 00:11:41.264
And of course I'm going to
choose that over basketball.

00:11:41.264 --> 00:11:43.294
And I did, and I've been
doing it ever since.

00:11:43.294 --> 00:11:45.619
- [Interviewer] So would you
say that was your big break

00:11:45.619 --> 00:11:47.525
or was there a stage a
little further down the line

00:11:47.525 --> 00:11:51.375
that was a significant
break for your music?

00:11:51.375 --> 00:11:54.734
- I would say my big break
is that point in time

00:11:54.734 --> 00:11:58.359
I learned that Stevie Wonder riff.

00:11:58.359 --> 00:12:00.158
That was one of the steps

00:12:00.158 --> 00:12:01.949
'cause I felt like man if I learn that

00:12:01.949 --> 00:12:03.224
I could learn anything.

00:12:03.224 --> 00:12:05.809
'Cause that guy was going pretty fast.

00:12:05.809 --> 00:12:06.950
But as far as crowd-wise
and what nailed it,

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:10.489
But as far as crowd-wise
and what nailed it,

00:12:10.489 --> 00:12:13.971
I would say my first
talent show pretty much

00:12:13.971 --> 00:12:15.508
is what bit me in a way,

00:12:15.508 --> 00:12:17.408
is what bit me in a way,

00:12:17.408 --> 00:12:19.931
like Peter Parker got bit by the spider

00:12:19.931 --> 00:12:21.238
like Peter Parker got bit by the spider

00:12:21.238 --> 00:12:22.543
and became Spider Man.

00:12:22.543 --> 00:12:24.394
That was the bite for me.

00:12:24.394 --> 00:12:27.842
When the women and everybody
was showing me so much love

00:12:27.842 --> 00:12:30.098
at the talent show and I won.

00:12:30.098 --> 00:12:31.335
And I was like wow.

00:12:31.335 --> 00:12:33.149
It was overwhelming.

00:12:33.149 --> 00:12:37.230
- When did you know that
you wanted to be a comedian?

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:40.247
Were you really young or
were you a little older?

00:12:40.247 --> 00:12:41.793
- I was young, I was in high school.

00:12:41.793 --> 00:12:43.194
And I knew I wasn't going to college

00:12:43.194 --> 00:12:44.482
'cause I barely got out of high school.

00:12:44.482 --> 00:12:45.901
I said, I better find
something right quick.

00:12:45.901 --> 00:12:47.019
So what am I good at?

00:12:47.019 --> 00:12:48.494
I was making people laugh

00:12:48.494 --> 00:12:49.916
and I was like why are you all laughing?

00:12:49.916 --> 00:12:50.749
They was like,

00:12:50.749 --> 00:12:51.749
"You're funny, you remind
me of Eddie Murphy."

00:12:51.749 --> 00:12:53.419
So I said, let me try this out.

00:12:53.419 --> 00:12:55.471
I hosted my talent show in high school

00:12:55.471 --> 00:12:57.926
and I got my first laugh
and I got an epiphany.

00:12:57.926 --> 00:12:59.826
And I was like, I'mma do this.
- Yeah.

00:12:59.826 --> 00:13:01.699
- 'Cause it's fun and I'm already,

00:13:01.699 --> 00:13:03.418
so that's when I found out.

00:13:03.418 --> 00:13:05.039
I hosted my first talent show.

00:13:05.039 --> 00:13:06.635
I hosted a talent show in high school

00:13:06.635 --> 00:13:08.033
and I said that's what I want to do.

00:13:08.033 --> 00:13:10.511
- The alarm clock would go off

00:13:10.511 --> 00:13:12.301
very early every single morning.

00:13:12.301 --> 00:13:14.517
I'd wake up, I'd check
my phone immediately

00:13:14.517 --> 00:13:16.840
for any emails that had come in.

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:20.600
And then it'd be shower,
shave, dress in my full suit,

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:21.433
And then it'd be shower,
shave, dress in my full suit,

00:13:21.433 --> 00:13:23.377
and jump in a car.

00:13:23.377 --> 00:13:24.697
And that car to me

00:13:24.697 --> 00:13:26.213
represented my first kind of
drudgery task for the day.

00:13:26.213 --> 00:13:29.498
represented my first kind of
drudgery task for the day.

00:13:29.498 --> 00:13:31.192
It made me feel trapped

00:13:31.192 --> 00:13:33.304
because I'd done all the right things.

00:13:33.304 --> 00:13:34.699
I had gone to college,

00:13:34.699 --> 00:13:37.561
I had been an officer in
the army for eight years,

00:13:37.561 --> 00:13:39.512
I had gone to corporate finance,

00:13:39.512 --> 00:13:41.429
I had worked with John Hancock,

00:13:41.429 --> 00:13:42.856
I had done commercial real estate.

00:13:42.856 --> 00:13:44.886
I had done all the right things.

00:13:44.886 --> 00:13:46.254
And now here I was

00:13:46.254 --> 00:13:48.959
stuck on this hamster wheel going nowhere,

00:13:48.959 --> 00:13:52.173
inspiring nobody, especially not myself,

00:13:52.173 --> 00:13:54.401
and just feeling like I was trapped

00:13:54.401 --> 00:13:56.366
in this world that I had created.

00:13:56.366 --> 00:13:58.370
And it was a sinking pit in my stomach.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:13:59.950
And I just was wondering why?

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:02.009
Why have I not found what I'm looking for

00:14:02.009 --> 00:14:02.842
when I've done everything

00:14:02.842 --> 00:14:04.979
that I was told I was supposed to do?

00:14:04.979 --> 00:14:07.097
Here I am years later,

00:14:07.097 --> 00:14:08.524
on the same hamster wheel

00:14:08.524 --> 00:14:11.133
feeling like I'm even further behind

00:14:11.133 --> 00:14:13.643
where I thought I was five year ago.

00:14:13.643 --> 00:14:16.429
And this sinking mundane
feeling would just not go away.

00:14:16.429 --> 00:14:18.966
It was ever-present with me.

00:14:18.966 --> 00:14:20.971
And I just wanted freedom.

00:14:20.971 --> 00:14:23.654
And I just wanted freedom.

00:14:23.654 --> 00:14:25.161
And I just wanted freedom.

00:14:25.161 --> 00:14:27.855
I just wanted to do work
that I was inspired by.

00:14:27.855 --> 00:14:32.022
And I just wanted to do
work that inspired others.

00:14:39.902 --> 00:14:43.227
So there I was, stuck in traffic again.

00:14:43.227 --> 00:14:47.058
But at least I had my
podcasts, or so I thought.

00:14:47.058 --> 00:14:49.508
Then, before I knew it, poof.

00:14:49.508 --> 00:14:51.073
My last podcast had ended.

00:14:51.073 --> 00:14:54.626
And I scrolled through my iPod
and there was nothing left.

00:14:54.626 --> 00:14:55.917
And I thought to myself,

00:14:55.917 --> 00:14:59.021
“Man, I have to sit here for
another 45 minutes in traffic,

00:14:59.021 --> 00:15:01.125
with nothing but the radio?”

00:15:01.125 --> 00:15:03.984
I was devastated, but at that moment,

00:15:03.984 --> 00:15:05.901
at that devastation moment,

00:15:05.901 --> 00:15:08.523
that is truly when my
a-ha moment happened.

00:15:08.523 --> 00:15:09.862
That’s when the light bulb went off.

00:15:09.862 --> 00:15:13.041
I said “What? There’s not
a seven-day-a-week podcast?

00:15:13.041 --> 00:15:14.707
"There should be a podcast

00:15:14.707 --> 00:15:17.427
"that comes out every
single day of the week,

00:15:17.427 --> 00:15:20.145
"that interviews inspiring
and successful entrepreneurs.”

00:15:20.145 --> 00:15:22.816
And that’s when I had
my light bulb moment.

00:15:22.816 --> 00:15:26.048
I said “There should be someone
that creates it, why not me?

00:15:26.048 --> 00:15:27.928
"I know all these great entrepreneurs

00:15:27.928 --> 00:15:29.543
"who are hosts of their own shows,

00:15:29.543 --> 00:15:31.900
"I could be just like
them, I can do this.”

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:35.160
So I had all of these
thoughts swirling in my head.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:38.047
“Am I going to fail, am I
going to look like a fool

00:15:38.047 --> 00:15:39.360
"in front of my friends and family,

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:42.891
"who up to this point had
only seen me as a success.”

00:15:42.891 --> 00:15:44.074
And these were real fears.

00:15:44.074 --> 00:15:46.840
I used to wake up sweating
in the middle of the night,

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:48.332
saying “What am I doing?

00:15:48.332 --> 00:15:50.007
"This is insane.”

00:15:50.007 --> 00:15:52.842
And the only way that I would
be able to go back to sleep

00:15:52.842 --> 00:15:55.573
was by convincing myself that
when I woke up in the morning,

00:15:55.573 --> 00:15:57.290
I was going to give it all up

00:15:57.290 --> 00:16:00.020
and go crawling back to my
job in commercial real estate.

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:02.503
But luckily for me, I would
wake up in the morning,

00:16:02.503 --> 00:16:03.834
the sun would be shining,

00:16:03.834 --> 00:16:04.728
and I’d say “You know what,

00:16:04.728 --> 00:16:07.143
"I’m going to give it one more day.

00:16:07.143 --> 00:16:09.351
"One more day, I’m going to sit down,

00:16:09.351 --> 00:16:12.647
"I’m going to learn what it
takes to upload a media file.

00:16:12.647 --> 00:16:15.766
"I’m going to learn how
to create great audio.

00:16:15.766 --> 00:16:17.449
"I’m going to learn what it
takes to be an interviewer,

00:16:17.449 --> 00:16:18.665
"a host of a show.”

00:16:18.665 --> 00:16:22.089
And every single day
I would get shot down,

00:16:22.089 --> 00:16:25.863
I would struggle, I would
come up against another wall

00:16:25.863 --> 00:16:28.344
that would knock me down,
but I kept getting up.

00:16:28.344 --> 00:16:31.355
I kept taking one step
forward for every half-step

00:16:31.355 --> 00:16:32.725
that I was taking back.

00:16:32.725 --> 00:16:33.743
And slowly but surely,

00:16:33.743 --> 00:16:36.416
I saw myself turning into a podcaster,

00:16:36.416 --> 00:16:38.219
right before my very own eyes.

00:16:38.219 --> 00:16:40.049
And it was a slow process,

00:16:40.049 --> 00:16:44.009
but it did come and I was able
to continue to move forward,

00:16:44.009 --> 00:16:48.192
until the launch of Entrepreneur
On Fire on September 22nd.

00:16:48.192 --> 00:16:52.192
'Cause at that point,
there was no turning back.

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:56.098
Fire Nation, look at what we’ve created.

00:16:56.098 --> 00:16:59.473
Look at the inspiration we’ve
spread throughout this world.

00:16:59.473 --> 00:17:01.870
A podcast, seven days a week,

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:04.273
interviewing the most inspiring

00:17:04.273 --> 00:17:06.917
and successful entrepreneurs in the world.

00:17:06.917 --> 00:17:07.750
Seth Godin, Guy Kawasaki,
Tim Ferriss, Gary Vaynerchuk.

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:11.616
Seth Godin, Guy Kawasaki,
Tim Ferriss, Gary Vaynerchuk.

